on/19e17dcaaf2db3eea98292a6dee56e6624d1957c483fb7d61a2ea5fb35b92775" "q-117084/selection/c486cb1648ded707f924f13a2c6fe38b050a34e02a9ef8498846f344da5fb9cd" "q-117084/selection/59bd0023a639c690c9f557842533403fc9a5583f6a02e073f918ee4a9f0b4c43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117084" :question/id #uuid "d5e9656c-2992-5d25-9ed1-710bfe400433" :question/math-academy-id "q-117084" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=81?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=3,$ and $r=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,3)$ and its radius is $9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117084/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection/aa11d709e8ef3c10d7bdf12d3b06de0fa2e26ee5e583d1d11ca64ab1f9577376" :answer/id #uuid "b7e51390-2c92-595d-b4a7-e47b4f0a7f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection/ad368024874ee77cb5996a2fc4953803af607eb1111a13910d1f4ea9e2f2f38a" :answer/id #uuid "231d7401-393d-52c1-8e3c-2f29675f718c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection/1602691fa9499f67010302395115cca8a17021534d61b6e623ac2d07562fd4f5" :answer/id #uuid "2afa30af-764b-5555-b930-b81c3e13fbc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection/c30d02d69f383c5c280e49b82dc56b093fd6f5acc052ef9d7d103ef659ee73cd" :answer/id #uuid "3ac6739e-cf6f-52ec-8481-099d7d5496ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection/8022631b92ee337dccbfcea6596d5c8a6e2532ac66311fe7b19d1e3287f4b643" :answer/id #uuid "24703135-38c0-5199-acb3-64c112199914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "46f257a2-b90f-51a3-829a-55339f9fc72e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117103/selection/ad368024874ee77cb5996a2fc4953803af607eb1111a13910d1f4ea9e2f2f38a" :answer-field/choices ["q-117103/selection/aa11d709e8ef3c10d7bdf12d3b06de0fa2e26ee5e583d1d11ca64ab1f9577376" "q-117103/selection/ad368024874ee77cb5996a2fc4953803af607eb1111a13910d1f4ea9e2f2f38a" "q-117103/selection/1602691fa9499f67010302395115cca8a17021534d61b6e623ac2d07562fd4f5" "q-117103/selection/c30d02d69f383c5c280e49b82dc56b093fd6f5acc052ef9d7d103ef659ee73cd" "q-117103/selection/8022631b92ee337dccbfcea6596d5c8a6e2532ac66311fe7b19d1e3287f4b643"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117103" :question/id #uuid "602e9979-5e3e-5ec8-b77b-59541ff9a767" :question/math-academy-id "q-117103" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/08653e0cdc9bb404bd7ef193dfc9f1b5c0884002e83dd72cbcbda5779a2363a1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,-1)$ and $(2,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,-1)$ and $Y(2,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(2,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(2,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
